# S8-7c: TIMED arm A (the four-seat control), second run of the paired timing ABAB of four seats against eight, on coding text (audits OFF, the pinned sampler in the verify trace).
# Arms alternate A B A B in this one image, each after its own all-four reset, the same prompts and the same admission order: A = c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace
# (production recipe plus the gate limits, four seats: the control; differs from the B arm by QWEN_FAST_M3_BLOCKS and the seat values only), B = c2-packed-tp4-8-time-gate (eight seats on two blocks). Second of two A runs, in the QUALIFICATION: the full ABAB is S8-7a, S8-7b, S8-7c, S8-7d.
# The tests: warmup, coding, concurrent4_code_equal (four 4k code prompts), concurrent4_code_32k (four 32k), concurrent8_code (eight, 4k to 24k) and
# concurrent8_code_32k (eight 32k). 800 tokens out each, started together. On the four-seat arm users 5 to 8 queue (that is what is measured).
# READ: judge the arms PAIRED per round, never by unpaired medians; check the load average around the run (a busy host skews host phases 10 to 20%)
# and repeat before believing a small gap. Per seat: the client rate and the steady rate, min / p10 / p50, with tau per seat; and the [PACKED-PHASE]
# per-block trace split (acceptance_report.block_trace_split): the second block's trace as a share of the round is what decides a 128-row block.
# BARS (a) at four or fewer live the eight-seat profile's paired round is at most 1.05 x the four-seat profile's; (b) at 8 live the aggregate is at
# least 1.0 x the four-seat four-live aggregate on the first four of the same prompts (between 0.85 and 1.0 only with the user's sign-off), and users 5
# to 8 see no decode-queue wait; (c) reported: per seat against the earlier G1-8 figure and the four-seat baseline.
# KILL SIGNAL (the driver stops the window and runs the handback): the median 8-live round above 2 x P(4) + 10 ms (P(4) the four-seat arm's median four-live
# round), or the 8-live aggregate below 0.85 x the four-live one. Two blocks then interfere or cost aggregate, and a single 128-row block or the round
# levers come before eight seats are served.
# OPTIONAL: its product is the numbers. A hang on a timed arm is a finding (the eight-seat arm is audits-off: the diag arm S8-3 is the hang evidence).
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; engine build 10-20 min on a warm cache (30 the first time a profile compiles); the six tests 30-55 min.
# SHIP WINDOW: the second pair of the ABAB (the first, v262 and v263, measured on the pre-ship image). OPTIONAL: its product is the numbers; the
# driver reads the kill rule and the bars from them. The first pair read bar (a) passing and bar (b) at about 0.86 of the four-live aggregate, which
# is inside the band that needs the owner's recorded sign-off.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-seats8 SHIP window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/seats8 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's stop rule, its minutes and the GO rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-8 is the SHIPPING image: the base SB8 builds
# from this branch with the eight-seat profile baked in as its serving default (ENV QWEN_C2_PROFILE) and the platform session cap baked as its
# seat count (ENV THATCH_SERVING_SESSION_CAP). Every job serves that one image, so the bytes that pass are the bytes that ship. Each job still
# names its profile explicitly, so none relies on the baked default. A commit that changes a file the image carries needs a new SB8 build and a
# new tag in every template.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-8
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4_code_equal,concurrent4_code_32k,concurrent8_code,concurrent8_code_32k
